WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:10.260
Skee-ball is my life. I met my wife playing skee-ball. Skee-ball has had a material impact on my life,

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:15.140
and I want to share that with others. And this space will be a conduit for that.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:20.160
Joey Mucha is a three-time skee-ball national champion and the owner of Joey the Cat,

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.880
an arcade rental repair and events company that he started in 2010.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:30.320
Building my business started out as a side project to my day job. I bought at that skee-ball machine on eBay

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:36.000
to practice and then had to learn how to repair it. So the natural progression was to put it in a bar,

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.580
see if it could make some recurring revenue, and then use that money to buy another skee-ball machine.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:45.360
In 2014 Mucha purchased this warehouse in San Francisco's Mission District

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:51.980
as a repair and storage facility. In 2019 he decided to convert it into an arcade and restaurant,

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:55.880
which should have been a straightforward process since the property was already zoned

00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:01.480
for commercial use. But a community activist incurring nothing more than a $600 fee

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:08.040
was able to temporarily scuttle Mucha's plans, forcing him to spend months rallying community support

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:15.840
and pleading his case at a public hearing. Joey the Cat's new outpost is slated to open in spring of 2021.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:21.040
But the story of how the project was nearly stopped, and what Mucha endured in order to prevail

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:27.600
underscores how even the most benign land-use changes in San Francisco can be hampered by red tape.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:33.120
It's a root cause of the city's housing crisis and jeopardizes San Francisco's competitiveness

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:37.360
over the long term. Joey the Cat should be renamed Joey the liar.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:43.060
This is within 500 feet of an elementary school. We're talking about proximity to schools,

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:46.580
we don't need young people walking by that and seeing these negative toxic images.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:51.560
I'm not converting this to a private event space only for corporates, I'm converting this to a public space

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:56.420
that can be used by all. In a perfect world if there was no red tape we would have been open six months ago.

00:01:56.420 --> 00:02:02.160
Mucha's troubles started when Kevin Ortiz, a local activist affiliated with the anti-gentrification group,

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:07.640
Cultural Action Network, filed an application for discretionary review, a process through which

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:12.360
any member of the public can ask the San Francisco Planning Commission to review an application

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:18.020
for a building permit. Neither Ortiz nor Cultural Action Network responded to our interview requests.

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:23.360
Even though these reviews are supposed to be used only under exceptional and extraordinary circumstances

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:27.160
they've become a regular part of the city's land use process.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:31.960
For example, the owner of a falafel restaurant was able to delay the opening of a competitor

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:37.580
by claiming that the neighborhood already had enough falafel. This homes third floor addition was blocked

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:42.760
on the grounds that it wasn't sufficiently Victorian. The conversion of a laundromat to an apartment building

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:49.040
has been delayed for over five years due in part to its casting a shadow on an already shaded school yard.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:55.800
So far in 2019 the Planning Commission publicly heard 91 requests for discretionary review.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:02.060
Because every building permit in the city is subject to this process. It adds enormous cost to construction,

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:05.040
exacerbating the city's severe housing shortage.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.760
Mucha prevailed by devoting enormous time to winning over community support,

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:12.400
which otherwise would have gone into running his business.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:17.940
I've basically become a politician, which I don't want to become. And I don't want that for anyone.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:23.020
I've watched a bunch of Planning Commission hearings and research to kind of understand the concept,

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:28.740
because small business owners shouldn't be flung into this process and expected to be perfect at this

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:32.740
when the activists are going to these almost weekly.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:36.420
I've gotten a profile on all the different planning commissioners, I know their names.

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:42.160
I know kind of what they vote for and against. My team and I went and garnered as much support as we could

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:46.000
from the community and we've worked with architects and had to figure out

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:52.280
how to make this space work for both what I want it to be and what is legally permitted

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:58.920
and make good business sense out of it. And finding that triangulation is incredibly complex and challenging

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:04.280
and has been very burdensome process for a small business owner.

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:08.280
Mucha went door-to-door in the mission asking for help from his neighbors.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:12.520
At the hearing more than twice as many supporters as opponents came out to  speak.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:14.900
Joey the Cat is fun for both adults and children,

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:20.480
and more importantly it is kept clean and it is a safe environment,

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:23.920
which is more than I can say for some of the parks and our neighborhood.

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:28.840
Political connections also came into play. Mucha received a letter of support from California

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:34.480
State Treasurer Fiona Ma, who once held a fundraiser at Joey's arcade. On a principled level

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:40.020
I think it's so hard for a small business owner to be successful in this city and when you start to layer on

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:45.540
red tape, or these hurdles and roadblocks that come out of personal interests or community interests

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:52.340
that don't necessarily align with the business, it makes it very difficult. And I think it's something

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:55.720
that should be changed at a policy level.

